{
  "description": "Semantic format mapping: format keyword validation for date-time, date, email, uri, uuid, ipv4, ipv6. `format` is an ANNOTATION, not an assertion — a non-conforming value MUST still validate; warning on it is SHOULD-level, which is what the warn_logged signal records. Authority: type-mapping §11.1. PROTOCOL_SPEC §4.15 carries the same rule as two edge-case rows.",
  "driver_contract": {
    "valid": "The `valid` expectation is normative and MUST be driven on the module-invocation path (the SDK's schema conversion + validator). `format` is an annotation, not an assertion (JSON Schema 2020-12 §7.2.1, type-mapping §11.1): a non-conforming value MUST NOT fail validation, and an unrecognised format MUST pass silently.",
    "warn_logged": "NOT normative across SDKs, and NOT a statement about module invocation. Where the SHOULD-level warning is emitted differs: apcore-typescript and apcore-python emit it on the module-invocation path; apcore-rust computes format warnings only in SchemaValidator::validate_detailed, which module invocation never reaches, so a Rust module call emits no format warning. Drivers satisfy this half by calling the warning path directly. Do not read a passing run as proof that all three warn during a module call.",
    "format_mappings": "Reference metadata for SDK implementors, NOT an assertion. It records the language-native type each `format` could map to; no SDK currently performs that mapping — apcore-python's generate_model() annotates a `format: date-time` field as `str`, not `datetime`. Runners MUST ignore it."
  },
  "format_mappings": {
    "date-time": {
      "python": "datetime.datetime",
      "typescript": "Date",
      "rust": "chrono::DateTime<Utc>"
    },
    "date": {
      "python": "datetime.date",
      "typescript": "string (ISO 8601 date)",
      "rust": "chrono::NaiveDate"
    },
    "time": {
      "python": "datetime.time",
      "typescript": "string (ISO 8601 time)",
      "rust": "chrono::NaiveTime"
    },
    "email": {
      "python": "pydantic.EmailStr",
      "typescript": "string (format-validated)",
      "rust": "String (regex-validated)"
    },
    "uri": {
      "python": "pydantic.AnyUrl",
      "typescript": "URL",
      "rust": "url::Url"
    },
    "uuid": {
      "python": "uuid.UUID",
      "typescript": "string (UUID regex)",
      "rust": "uuid::Uuid"
    },
    "ipv4": {
      "python": "IPv4Address",
      "typescript": "string (format-validated)",
      "rust": "std::net::Ipv4Addr"
    },
    "ipv6": {
      "python": "IPv6Address",
      "typescript": "string (format-validated)",
      "rust": "std::net::Ipv6Addr"
    }
  },
  "test_cases": [
    {
      "id": "datetime_valid_iso8601",
      "description": "Valid ISO 8601 datetime string with UTC offset — must be accepted",
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "occurred_at": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "occurred_at"
        ]
      },
      "input": {
        "occurred_at": "2026-04-28T12:00:00Z"
      },
      "expected": {
        "valid": true,
        "warn_logged": false,
        "error_code": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "datetime_invalid",
      "description": "Plaintext string where date-time is expected — format enforcement is SHOULD-level so this produces a warning, not a hard error",
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "occurred_at": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "occurred_at"
        ]
      },
      "input": {
        "occurred_at": "not-a-date"
      },
      "expected": {
        "valid": true,
        "warn_logged": true,
        "error_code": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "date_valid",
      "description": "Valid ISO 8601 date string — must be accepted",
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "birthday": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "birthday"
        ]
      },
      "input": {
        "birthday": "2026-04-28"
      },
      "expected": {
        "valid": true,
        "warn_logged": false,
        "error_code": null
      }
    },
    {
